me:kht,reset_main_brush_work_time:Sht,reset_sensor_dirty_time:xht,reset_side_brush_work_time:Cht,resetConsumables_description:Eht,resume_segment_clean:Tht,resume_zoned_clean:Aht,"roborock adapter settings":"Adapter settings for roborock",rss:zht,rtsp:Iht,save_furnitures:Oht,sensor_dirty_time:Mht,set_carpet_clean_mode:Rht,set_carpet_mode:Dht,set_clean_sequence:Nht,set_custom_mode:Pht,set_dust_collection_mode:jht,set_dust_collection_switch_status:Lht,set_mop_mode:Fht,set_smart_wash_params:Bht,set_wash_towel_mode:qht,set_water_box_custom_mode:Wht,side_brush_life:Hht,side_brush_work_time:Uht,"Saved program execution":"Saved program execution","Local adapter queue":"Local adapter queue","Cloud like Roborock app":"Cloud like Roborock app","Local: runs the saved scene locally from its Roborock scene steps and keeps the local queue/resume. Cloud: starts the saved scene through Roborock cloud like the app. No automatic fallback between modes.":"Local: runs the saved scene locally from its Roborock scene steps and keeps the local queue/resume. Cloud: starts the saved scene through Roborock cloud like the app. No automatic fallback between modes.",split_segment:Vht,start_cleaning_time:Ght,start_type:Xht,state:Kht,stop_segment_clean:Yht,stop_zoned_clean:Jht,strainer_work_times:Zht,stream_html:Qht,stream_mp4:e_t,switch_map_mode:t_t,"United States":"United States",unsave_map_flag:n_t,unsave_map_reason:o_t,"Update interval":"Update Interval","Update interval while cleaning":"Update interval while cleaning","Seconds between two polls while the robot is cleaning, returning or washing. Lower values make position, area and progress follow more closely, but every poll is a request: they cost network traffic and load on both the robot and ioBroker. Below about 3 seconds the gain is barely visible.":"Seconds between two polls while the robot is cleaning, returning or washing. Lower values make position, area and progress follow more closely, but every poll is a request: they cost network traffic and load on both the robot and ioBroker. Below about 3 seconds the gain is barely visible.","Maximum wait after failed polls":"Maximum wait after failed polls","After a failed poll the adapter waits 30 seconds, then doubles the wait after each further failure, up to this limit. A low value notices a returning robot sooner but keeps retrying against an unreachable device; a high value keeps the log and the network quiet during a longer outage.":"After a failed poll the adapter waits 30 seconds, then doubles the wait after each further failure, up to this limit. A low value notices a returning robot sooner but keeps retrying against an unreachable device; a high value keeps the log and the network quiet during a longer outage.","Live map update":"Live map update","Seconds between two checks for map changes while the robot is cleaning; while it stands still the adapter waits twice as long. The check itself is a small request that asks only what changed, and a complete map is transferred only when something actually did - so a low value costs far less than it looks, but it is still one request per interval on the robot, the network and ioBroker. Robots that do not offer the incremental map have to transfer the whole map every time and are therefore never checked faster than every 5 seconds. 0 switches the live update off; the map is then only refreshed by the normal poll.":"Seconds between two checks for map changes while the robot is cleaning; while it stands still the adapter waits twice as long. The check itself is a small request that asks only what changed, and a complete map is transferred only when something actually did - so a low value costs far less than it looks, but it is still one request per interval on the robot, the network and ioBroker. Robots that do not offer the incremental map have to transfer the whole map every time and are therefore never checked faster than every 5 seconds. 0 switches the live update off; the map is then only refreshed by the normal poll.","Seconds between two polls while the robot is idle or docked. Nothing changes in this state, so a long interval costs nothing; a short one only adds network traffic and load on the robot and on ioBroker.":"Seconds between two polls while the robot is idle or docked. Nothing changes in this state, so a long interval costs nothing; a short one only adds network traffic and load on the robot and on ioBroker.",wash_count:r_t,wash_phase:a_t,wash_ready:s_t,wash_status:i_t,water_shortage_status:c_t,webserverPort:l_t,"Account & connection":"Account & connection",Map:"Map",Advanced:u_t,"Local operation":"Local operation",'With "Email + 2FA Code" Roborock sends a six digit code by email. There is no input field for it here: enter the code into the state roborock.<instance>.loginCode within 15 minutes of starting the adapter.':'With "Email + 2FA Code" Roborock sends a six digit code by email. There is no input field for it here: enter the code into the state roborock.<instance>.loginCode within 15 minutes of starting the adapter.',"Connection mode":"Connection mode","Cloud and local":"Cloud and local","Local only (no cloud contact)":"Local only (no cloud contact)","Local only: the adapter never contacts the Roborock cloud. This requires manually configured devices with duid and localKey. Cloud based functions stay unavailable in this mode - map retrieval currently needs the cloud connection, as do saved scenes, firmware information and camera streaming. There is no automatic fallback to the cloud.":"Local only: the adapter never contacts the Roborock cloud. This requires manually configured devices with duid and localKey. Cloud based functions stay unavailable in this mode - map retrieval currently needs the cloud connection, as do saved scenes, firmware information and camera streaming. There is no automatic fallback to the cloud.","Manual devices (JSON)":"Manual devices (JSON)",'JSON array, one object per device: {"duid": "...", "localKey": "...", "ip": "192.168.1.50", "pv": "1.0"}. Optional: name, model, category, sn. The localKey is a 16 character device secret that only exists in the Roborock cloud device list and cannot be derived locally; it changes only when the device is paired again. Log in once with your account to read it, then keep it here. It is stored encrypted and never written to the log.':'JSON array, one object per device: {"duid": "...", "localKey": "...", "ip": "192.168.1.50", "pv": "1.0"}. Optional: name, model, category, sn. The localKey is a 16 character device secret that only exists in the Roborock cloud device list and cannot be derived locally; it changes only when the device is paired again. Log in once with your account to read it, then keep it here. It is stored encrypted and never written to the log.',"Search devices in network":"Search devices in network","Listens for device broadcasts and reports duid, IP address and protocol version, so a manual entry can be created without a cloud account. The adapter instance must be running.":"Listens for device broadcasts and reports duid, IP address and protocol version, so a manual entry can be created without a cloud account. The adapter instance must be running.","Listen for device broadcasts (UDP 58866)":"Listen for device broadcasts (UDP 58866)","Off: only devices with a statically configured IP address are used. Helpful when broadcasts are filtered (VLAN, WLAN client isolation, LXC or Docker bridges).":"Off: only devices with a statically configured IP address are used. Helpful when broadcasts are filtered (VLAN, WLAN client isolation, LXC or Docker bridges).","Network interface for discovery":"Network interface for discovery","JSON array of { duid, localKey, ip, pv }. The localKey is a device secret and is stored encrypted.":"JSON array of { duid, localKey, ip, pv }. The localKey is a device secret and is stored encrypted.",ui_device:d_t,ui_floor:p_t,ui_fan_power:h_t,ui_mop_mode:__t,ui_water_flow:m_t,ui_clean_mode_vac_and_mop:f_t,ui_clea